// Word cards (Wing 1 + Wing 2): what the player learns, one card per word (docs/MEMORY_SYSTEM.md). DRAFT glosses — every
// English and Urdu meaning here needs the reviewer's sign-off before release (PLAN D8). Written fresh; nothing is
// copied from the reference booklets.
//   ar     the word as taught, in isolation (not Qur'anic text; ayat always come verbatim from Tanzil)
//   units  corpus units this card stands for (scripts/lib/corpus.mjs); drives the coverage meter. A card also
//          carries forms the corpus lists apart (plural آبَاء, feminine كَبِيرَة, light لٰكِنْ) so they count once learned
//   pic    emoji stand-in for the picture language (VISUAL_GAMES §1); `medal` = calligraphy only, no picture
//          ("scroll:…" parchment for prophets, angels, revealed books; "plain:…" ink only, e.g. Shaytan)
//   g      { en, ur } short meaning; "a; b" = two different senses
//   say    optional: how to say the word, in Latin letters. Leave it out: the build spells it by rule from the vowel
//          marks (scripts/lib/translit.mjs). Write it only where the rule cannot work (the letter names الٓمٓ) or reads
//          wrong. Shown only when the player turns on "Show how to say it".
//   twin   the other card, or a list of cards, that looks or reads the same to the player: the same Arabic (وَ "and" /
//          وَ "by"), or the same caption in English or Urdu as the game compares captions (جَاءَ / أَتَى "come"; also
//          "this" / "this (she-word)": words in brackets do not count, core/options.js captionKey). Cards name each
//          other. Twins are never offered as a wrong answer to each other, and the build fails on any unmarked pair
//          (scripts/lib/checks.mjs). To let two such words be asked against each other, word them apart outside brackets

